.*
.* Help modules and the text markup they carry, together with the
.* comment line, the imbed directive and the symbols that stand for
.* characters the markup would otherwise read as its own.
.*
.* Member: PNLHELP
.* Source: Application Display Programming SC41-5715 (V6R1), appendix A.
.* Retrieved: 2026-07-28
.*
:pnlgrp schidx=ordidx enbgui=yes.
.*
.* A name defined elsewhere is brought in by IMPORT.
:import name=commonh pnlgrp=commonpg.
:import name=sharedh newname=localh pnlgrp=commonpg prdlib=mylib.
.*
.* From "Example: Hypertext Link" in the reference.
:HELP NAME='hyper/help'.Hypertext in i5/OS
:P.
Hypertext lets users explore
the online help information in a way that is most
natural for them.
Hypertext links can be used within :LINK
PERFORM='DSPHELP item/specific/help'
    .item specific help:ELINK.,
:LINK PERFORM='dsphelp extended/help'
    .extended help:ELINK., and
:LINK PERFORM='dsphelp index/search'
    .index search help:ELINK..
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='item/specific/help'
    .Definition of Item Specific Help
:P.
Item specific help is . . .
:EHELP.
.*
.* A link may be conditioned. UNLESSn and LINKWHEN take a
.* conditional expression, which joins the built-in functions
.* with the logical operators.
:help name='cond/help'.Conditioned links
:p.See :LINK PERFORM='DSPHELP extended/help'
   LINKWHEN='CHKUSRCLS(*SECOFR) *OR CHKPGM("MYLIB/MYPGM")'
   UNLESS1='*NOT CHKOBJ("MYLIB/ORDFILE","*FILE","*USE")'
   THENDO1='DSPHELP no/authority'
   .the extended help:ELINK.
:ehelp.
.*
.* From "Example: Heading Tags" in the reference.
:help name=headhlp.Headings
:H1.A One Heading
:p.Here's a paragraph.
:H2.A Two Heading
:p.Another paragraph.
:H3.A Three Heading
:p.Still another paragraph.
:H4.A Four Heading
:p.Still another paragraph.
.*
.* From "Example: Sample Headings" in the reference.
:XH1.Main Subject
:p.Here's a paragraph.
:XH2.Topic
:p.Another paragraph.
:XH3.Subtopic
:p.Still another paragraph.
:XH4.A Four Heading
:p.Still another paragraph.
:ehelp.
.*
.* From "Example: Paragraph Tag" in the reference.
.* and "Example: Using a Note".
:help name=parahlp.Paragraphs
:P.Here's a paragraph.
Lines are formatted to
fill the column.
:P.Here's another
paragraph.
:NT.
Here's the first paragraph
of the note.
:P.
Here's the second paragraph
of the note.
:ENT.
.*
.* From "Example: Paragraph Continuation" in the reference.
:p.If you enter the following
command
:xmp.
WRKSPLF
:exmp.
:pc.a listing of all my spool files
appears on the
terminal.
:ehelp.
