.*
.* From "Example: Sample Figure" in the reference.
.* with "Unformatted Lines" and "Formatting an Example".
:help name=fighlp.Figures
:FIG frame=rule.
some
   sample
      text
:FIGCAP.A Sample Figure
:EFIG.
:LINES.
First line
Second line
:ELINES.
:xmp.
This is an example
right here
:exmp.
.*
.* The remaining phrase tags: a highlighted phrase, a title
.* citation and reverse text.
:p.The :HP2.order number:EHP2. is required.
:p.See :CIT.Application Display Programming:ECIT. for more.
:p.Right to left text is written :RT.abc:ERT. this way.
:imhelp name=commonh.
:ehelp.
.*
.* From "Example: Index Search Synonyms" in the reference.
.* with the index search entry and subtopics they belong to.
:isch roots='order entry'.Entering an order
:ischsubt topics='hyper/help headhlp'.
:ISCHSYN ROOT='copy'.copy copying copies
:ISCHSYN ROOT='delete'.delete deleting deletes
:ISCHSYN ROOT='delete'.remove removes removing
:ISCHSYN ROOT='folder'.folder folders
.*
.* From "Examples: Translation List" in the reference.
:tl msgid=MMM0001 msgf='*LIBL/QCPFMSG'.
:ti value=1.Blue
:ti value=1.BLUE
:ti value=2.Red
:ti value=2.RED
:ti value=3.Green
:ti value=3.GREEN
:ti value=4.Turquoise
:ti value=4.TURQUOISE
:etl.
.*
.* A printed panel, and "Example: Trailer Message".
:prthead name=ordprth title='Order register' width=132 prtdate=yes prttime=yes.
:eprthead.
:prtpnl name=ordprt title='Orders' width=132.
:p.One line for each order.
:prttrail.E N D   O F   L I S T I N G
:eprtpnl.
:copyr.(C) Example Ltd 2026
.*
.* The symbols stand for characters the markup reads as its
.* own: an ampersand, a colon, a period and a message.
:help name=symhlp.Symbols
:p.Use &amp. for an ampersand and &colon. for a colon.
:p.A period is &period. and a soft line break is &slr.
:p.The message reads &msg(USR0001,USRMSG).
:p.A continued line ends with &cont.
:ehelp.
.*
.* The imbed directive brings in another member.
.im COMMONPG
:epnlgrp.
